UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 17, Lesson 3: Connectives for reasons', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Reason connectives such as because, so and therefore link a claim to its support and help readers follow the logic.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same strategy to an unfamiliar topic or audience, then compare the effect of two different choices.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nJoin these ideas with a suitable connective: \"Kits help memory. We should borrow more kits.\"\n\nFEEDBACK\nKits help memory, so / therefore we should borrow more kits. Or: We should borrow more kits because kits help memory.\n\nCHECK\nStacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nRewrite six short argument pairs using because, so or therefore appropriately. Label which word shows reason and which shows result for three examples.\n\nWrite a short reflection describing one specific revision you made and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"English","learning_intention":"Reason connectives such as because, so and therefore link a claim to its support and help readers follow the logic.","lesson_number":3,"lesson_role":"Language and spelling","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN2-VOCAB-01","EN2-SPELL-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Rewrite six short argument pairs using because, so or therefore appropriately. Label which word shows reason and which shows result for three examples. Accept equivalent 