 lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Stacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify.","Reason connectives such as because, so and therefore link a claim to its support and help readers follow the logic.","Kits help memory, so / therefore we should borrow more kits.","Careful use of therefore and explain why it matters with clear evidence."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with because?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named therefore and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Stacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify.","Name therefore and explain why it matters only, without linking it to because.","Apply because to new material and name the therefore and explain why it matters used."],"question":"Which response best applies because with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries because. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event.","Say the writing is good without naming any words.","Stacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify.","Point to exact words in the sentence that show because and say what they do."],"question":"Read: \"Under the pier, Sam found a locked tin and a dripping map.\" Which choice best uses because from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill with textual evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged.","Name therefore and explain why it matters without linking it to any words in the text.","Kits help memory, so / therefore we should borrow more kits.","Stacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify."],"question":"Which statement correctly applies the lesson idea about because?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Start from a specific textual clue, then explain its effect. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Lengthen the answer with adjectives while keeping the same idea.","Locate a specific word, phrase or structural clue before deciding.","Guess from the title alone with no textual clue.","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged."],"question":"In a new text, what should you do first to analyse therefore and explain why it matters?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Repair means fixing meaning or evidence, not padding. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Add adjectives without fixing the wrong idea.","Make the answer longer while keeping the same mistake.","Delete the evidence that disagreed with your first guess.","Change the inaccurate idea or missing evidence, not only the length."],"question":"Which revision actually improves meaning for because?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Accurate transfer needs fresh material with an explained language choice. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Stacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify.","Use a fresh sentence or text and explain one precise choice about because.","Retype the worked model as the final answer.","Change fonts and claim the work is new."],"question":"Which response shows accurate use of because on fresh material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about because with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating because on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using because on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for because. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with because, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: Stacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify.. Correction: Kits help memory, so / therefore we should borrow more kits.. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent task and reflection, with explanations where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-eng-y3-w17-l3","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA alignment; verify content points before acceptance.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise because.","Read the mission before you start writing or speaking.","Keep the audience and purpose in mind as you work."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reason with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the evidence."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the wording that carries the meaning.","Then explain the choice without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore the example.","Prefer evidence over wording that merely sounds clever."],"submit":["Check that your response and reason are both present.","Proofread names, sequence and punctuation.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact word or action before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and underline one useful detail.","Say what that detail helps a reader understand.","A vague compliment is weaker than quoted evidence."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with a stronger revision.","Change meaning or accuracy, not only length.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh topic that still uses the same skill.","Explain one decision in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include an original response and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new content."]},"subject":"English","success_criteria":["I can use because with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify therefore and explain why it matters.","I can practise so independently on a new prompt.","I can notice connective needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Reason connectives such as because, so and therefore link a claim to its support and help readers follow the logic.","options":["An answer copied without understanding.","Reason connectives such as because, so and therefore link a claim to its support and help readers follow the logic.","A guess with no explanation.","A claim unrelated to the text."],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about because with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\n\"We need shade sails because students wait in the sun; therefore the council should fund covers.\" Because explains; therefore shows a result.\n\nTRY FIRST\nJoin these ideas with a suitable connective: \"Kits help memory. We should borrow more kits.\"\n\nFEEDBACK\nKits help memory, so / therefore we should borrow more kits. Or: We should borrow more kits because kits help memory.","explain":"Reason connectives such as because, so and therefore link a claim to its support and help readers follow the logic.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Stacking many connectives in one sentence can confuse rather than clarify. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Reason and result connectives contrasted.","caption":"Choose the connective that matches the link.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">because</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">explains a reason</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">therefore</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">shows a result</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: \"We need shade sails because students wait in the sun; therefore the council should fund covers.\" Because explains; ther Then write your own attempt.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.\nJuno: Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: \"We need shade sails because students wait in the sun; therefore the council should fund covers.\" Because explains; ther Then write your own attempt."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.","options":["An answer copied without understanding.","Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does","A guess with no explanation.","A claim unrelated to the text."],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about because with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\n\"We need shade sails because students wait in the sun; therefore the council should fund covers.\" Because explains; therefore shows a result. Think about how this word or relationship creates meaning.\n\nTRY FIRST\nUnderline or quote one precise detail in the model and explain its effect.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning.","explain":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific